--- kps-S31ag finding (HYP-3093) ---
The COARSE (mod 14) winding tournament is DEGENERATE for EVERY k>=8 cluster.
Reason (exact pigeonhole): Z/14 has 7 antipodal pairs {r,r+7}; the pair {r,r+7} differs by 7,
and 7*a mod 14 in {0,7} for ALL phases a => a PERMANENT tie. Any k>=8 distinct residues mod 14
must (pigeonhole, 8>7) contain a full antipodal pair => no proper tournament exists.
THRESHOLD IS EXACTLY k=8 = the first binding LRC(14) row (cap_8 tightest).
=> the project's H-maximization (regular max H, THM-027) CANNOT directly prove the coverage
extremality at the coarse scale: the extremal clusters are tournament-degenerate. The apex-7
antipodal obstruction is pervasive exactly at the binding sizes. The H/tournament structure must
live at the FINE scale (mod p, p>14 prime, no antipodal ties): there the AP -> regular R_p, max H.
LIVE DIRECTION: connect coverage P(N=0)=lim(fine-scale good count) to the fine-scale winding
tournament's H-maximization (regular/Paley max H) -- the H-bridge re-opens at the fine scale.
